      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "chem170_full_step364",
          "description": "Reference: the chem_opt = 170 full-column capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_full.sh: the reference namelist with emiss_opt = 4, emiss_inpt_opt = 101, bio_emiss_opt = 1, wetscav_onoff = -1 and cu_physics = 0; fork ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170) at model step 364 (dt = 60 s, 12:04 LST), column (its, jts): local noon of the first day, the strongest photochemistry and emissions of the run. Grid-scale rain over the step 0 kg/m2; j(NO2) at the surface 0.00674 /s; Wesely iland 2, iseason 1, rh 38.7 %. The column state is CBM-Z's at KPP entry (var_in), and every expected value is the SUM, at that one state, of each process's instantaneous tendency from a real64 replay of the Fortran: Vdot of cbmz_mosaic_Fun (kernels/cbmz_driver); conv times the emissions_driver increment over dt (kernels/emissions_driver; independent of the chemical state); conv times vertmx with K = 0 -- the deposition flux through the ground alone -- with the ddvel dry_dep_driver hands it, extrapolated to dt -> 0 (Romberg on dt = 20 ... 2.5 s); and, for sulf, conv times wetdep_ls's increment over dt at this state (kernels/wetdep_ls_driver with the dumped call's gases replaced by it). conv = 1e-6 dens2con_a rho_phy is the KPP interface's own. Every species and every layer is asserted, rel 1e-10, with an absolute bound of 1e-05 of the layer's deposition term: the replayed vertmx reads WRF's real32 velocity, the column forms it through the Wesely components in double precision (their own tests compare at rel 1e-5).",
